       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day (2,550 mg for immediate-release in the US).\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 850 to 1000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose of this size raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), 1000 mg twice daily, or a total daily dose of 1700 mg split into two or three doses.\n\nPlease tell me the intended dose and frequency, and whether the formulation is immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter the order as soon as I have that. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm it explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
